&lt;p&gt;This is a country-lead role as the senior DCSE presence in Australia with a deliberate tilt toward security systems and systems architecture. You&#39;ll be the on-the-ground owner of day-to-day security operations for the region, and you&#39;ll also be the technical owner of the systems those operations run on: access control, video management, intrusion detection, and visitor management platforms and, just as importantly, the way they integrate. We want someone who thinks in data flows and system interfaces, not just devices You&#39;ll help design and build toward that architecture while keeping regional operations running with high reliability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with US-based security engineering and operations teams, with the time-zone offset as a feature: this role anchors coverage and escalation when the US is offline, and may help stand up a regional 24/7 monitoring capability as the program matures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the regional operations lead for data center physical security in Australia: run site security programs, coordinate with site operators and contract guard forces, and own in-region incident response and escalation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer and operate the region&#39;s electronic security systems&amp;nbsp; access control, video management (VMS), intrusion detection, and visitor management including configuration, health monitoring, and lifecycle management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and document security systems architecture: device schedules, integration points, data flows, and network topology for security infrastructure at new and existing sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain integrations that bring security data sources (video, access events, alarms, sensors) into centralized monitoring and analysis platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support construction-phase security for new builds and modular deployments in region: design reviews, commissioning of security systems, and security gates before handover&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage regional security vendors and integrators scoping, delivery quality, and accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and maintain the operational backbone: post orders, standard operating procedures, and audit-ready documentation for regional security controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide after-hours coverage and structured handoffs to US-based teams as part of follow-the-sun security operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience administering enterprise physical security systems, including access control platforms and video management systems (e.g., Genetec, Lenel, Milestone, C•CURE, or comparable)&lt;/li&gt;
