&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Manager, IT Support to lead our Americas support team. IT Support is the front door for every employee technology need at Anthropic: our Claude-backed support assistant, the human ticket queue behind it, walk-ups and desk-side help, hardware swaps, conference room triage, and a dedicated white-glove channel for our executives and board.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is first and foremost a people leadership role. You&#39;ll manage a team of IT Support Engineers across San Francisco, New York, and Seattle—hiring them, coaching them, and growing them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role goes beyond running a queue, too. Our support model is being rebuilt this year, and much of what you&#39;d normally inherit doesn&#39;t exist yet—you&#39;ll help shape the service levels this team is held to, and stand up the Americas leg of a follow-the-sun on-call rotation. You&#39;ll also hold a tension we take seriously: our engineers build the automation that keeps requests from ever reaching a person, and they treat the queue as the first priority, always. You&#39;ll partner closely with our specialist operations teams, IT Engineering, Security, People Operations, and Workplace to deliver an exceptional employee experience while maintaining the rigorous security posture our mission demands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop a team of IT Support Engineers across San Francisco, New York, and Seattle—1:1s, feedback, performance management, and career growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire IT Support Engineers, including for our executive and board support function, and raise the bar as the team grows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own in-office coverage and staffing across San Francisco, New York, and Seattle, and lead a team you aren&#39;t always in the same room with&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own queue health, service level attainment, and routing rules across the Americas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for how the Americas performs against our support metrics—first-touch resolution, time to first response, time to resolution, employee satisfaction—and drive the changes that move them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run and staff the Americas on-call rotation within the global follow-the-sun model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Route escalations into specialist operations teams and IT Engineering, and hold your team to those boundaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protect engineering time for automation and deflection work without letting the queue slip&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Workplace, People Ops, and other teams to support office operations and company events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel regularly to San Francisco and occasionally to Seattle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in IT support and operations, with 3+ years managing a support team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of managing and developing engineers: hiring, coaching, performance conversations that change behavior, and moving people into their next role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a frontline IT support team, including ownership of a queue, its service levels, and the people who work it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing across multiple offices, including reports you don&#39;t sit with, and a real answer for how you keep them developing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on IT support fundamentals: macOS-primary fleets, identity and access, SaaS troubleshooting, hardware lifecycle, and AV first-response&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A demonstrated ability to move a support function&#39;s metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A security-first mindset and excellent judgment about when user experience yields to security requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ambiguity and rapidly shifting priorities in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication—you can write a runbook, a postmortem, and a piece of hard feedback, and have each land&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Strong candidates may also have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building support infrastructure rather than inheriting it: a queue structure, an on-call rotation, an escalation model, or SLAs that didn&#39;t exist before you arrived&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting executives or a board to a white-glove standard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building support automation, ticket deflection programs, or self-service platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting AI/ML research environments or highly technical user bases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in companies with significant security or compliance requirements (e.g. SOC 2, FedRAMP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
